      "description": "TV Jr. brings the live TV and movies you already have to iPhone and HomeView, in one simple app. It doesn't include any channels of its own.\n\nPick from Home, Channels or Library at the top. Choose something and it opens full screen; close it and it keeps playing in the mini player while you browse.\n\n• HDHomeRun: find your tuner on Wi‑Fi and watch its antenna or cable channels, converted right on your iPhone. No DVR or server needed.\n• Jellyfin: watch the movies and shows in your Jellyfin library. Sign in with Quick Connect, see Continue Watching and Recently Added, and pick up where you left off. Your place is saved back to Jellyfin.\n• ErsatzTV: add your own custom channels in one tap.\n• HomeView: Home, Channels and Library on HomeView too, playing full screen.\n• What's on now: the current show and time left for HDHomeRun channels and playlists that publish a guide.\n• Playlists: import an M3U playlist from your home media server and pick the channels you want. Links refresh automatically.\n• Stream links: add a single live stream (.m3u8).\n• Favorites, Recent channels, and sources you can turn on or off and reorder.\n• iPhone Duo: open it up to watch on one side and browse on the other.\n• Captions on HDHomeRun channels, AirPlay, and Picture in Picture.\n• Light and dark mode. Your channels back up to your own iCloud.\n\nWhere streams come from: an HDHomeRun tuner on your network, your own Jellyfin or ErsatzTV server, your TV or internet provider, broadcasters that publish free live streams, or your own media server. Only add streams you have the right to watch.\n\nJellyfin is a trademark of the Jellyfin project; TV Jr. is not affiliated with it. Screenshots feature Big Buck Bunny and Tears of Steel, © Blender Foundation (blender.org), licensed under CC BY 3.0, and Caminandes, © Blender Foundation, licensed under CC BY.",
